for feedback: 
ASR word times can be ~0.3 s early. "downward turn" was reported ending at 1574.96 s but the waveform shows "turn" at 1575.10–1575.44, so a cut built from word times clipped it. Always check final-word boundaries against the waveform before trusting them.

How did you figure this out? How did you verify it?
